    "created_at": "2016-05-04T11:54:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-04T11:54:02Z",
    "body": "`prefetch` is for the next navigation, so it makes perfect sense to annotate a link you expect the user to follow with `prefetch`. However, the other keywords are not necessarily resources you would expect the user to navigate to -- e.g. preloading a stylesheet or DNS-resolving your CDN. So I tend to agree with @yoavweiss \n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
