    "created_at": "2016-05-04T15:27:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-04T15:27:10Z",
    "body": "I'd argue that `dns-prefetch` and `preconnect` are things that the browser can heuristically perform on it own for `<a>`/`<area>` (and some do in certain scenarios).\n\nRegarding `prefetch`/`prerender`, there's a slightly stronger case there to add a `rel` rather than include a full fledged `<link>` when they are the likely next page.\n\nI agree regarding it being low priority as far as implementation goes.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
