    "created_at": "2016-05-04T15:29:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-04T15:29:25Z",
    "body": "> I'd argue that dns-prefetch and preconnect are things that the browser can heuristically perform on it own for <a>/<area> (and some do in certain scenarios).\n\nSure, it can, but that's an orthogonal feature. The browser guesses, the developer can help the browser by indicating which things it _should_ perform those actions for.\n\n> Regarding prefetch/prerender, there's a slightly stronger case there to add a rel rather than include a full fledged <link> when they are the likely next page.\n\nEmphasis on slightly.. it's a minor convenience, in my books.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
