    "created_at": "2016-05-04T19:39:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-04T19:39:13Z",
    "body": "> I agree regarding it being low priority as far as implementation goes.\n\nThis to me suggests we should specify what is implemented today, and let developers use both `link` and `a` if they wanted to use `<a rel=presomething>`. We can then revisit it later if an implementor wants to add some more keywords to a/area, or we have data that a lot of Web pages are using link+a as a workaround or using only `<a rel=presomething>` and would be improved if browsers implemented it...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
