    "created_at": "2016-05-10T05:12:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T05:12:46Z",
    "body": "@domenic apologies about the delay. \n\nWe talked about this on last week's webperf call. Long story short: above is lgtm. \n\nThat said, we also left an open question as to whether even prefetch should be allowed on a/area. I just ran a couple of quick tests, and none of the browsers seem to honor prefetch on `a`'s:\n- Test page: http://output.jsbin.com/zacaqo/latest/quiet (view source)\n- Chrome, Firefox, IE 11 only respect link-rel-prefetch:\n  - Chrome: http://www.webpagetest.org/result/160510_XE_97M/1/details/\n  - Firefox: http://www.webpagetest.org/result/160510_DQ_97X/1/details/\n  - IE11: http://www.webpagetest.org/result/160510_54_98P/1/details/\n  - Safari doesn't trigger prefetch at all.\n  - ... postbin results: http://requestb.in/1ey2wwp1?inspect\n\nAs such, for sake of simplicity and sanity, perhaps we ought to remove prefetch as well?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
